      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "Diane Griffiths",
      "description": "The Cavern Club @The Cavern Pub, Liverpool, England\n\n\n               The Cavern Club\nBetween 1957 and 1973, most of the worlds leading artistes\nplayed at the Cavern Club. Although synonymous with the\nhistory of the Beatles, the Club hosted performances by the\ngreatest names in the history of jazz, rock, pop, blues and\nsoul. The club closed in 1973 only to re-open at its original\naddress of 10 Mathew Street (across the street from here)\nin 1984. The Club, although remoselled, still atracts world-\nwide media attension and   the 1990's great luminaries of\nthe British pop scene such as OASYS and DODGY have\nperformed there. The Cavern Pub and its exterior \"The\nCavern Wall of Fame\" is a tribute to those celebrated and\nrevered icons of twentieth century popular culture.",
      "dateCreated": "2014-12-17 18:28",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "the-cavern-club-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "gcmz"
    },
